==================================================================================
PARITY (web AcknowledgeAlertDialog.tsx -> native), no scope narrowing
==================================================================================
  Data sources (web -> native P1/S8 seam):
    useTranslation -> AckAlertStrings facade (P1/S10), no literals.
    useId          -> the hint is wired as the note field's a11y value (native VoiceOver
                      describedby), not an HTML id.
    onSubmit(note) -> AckAlertService.acknowledge(body) (async; no HTTP in the view) ->
                      AckAlertController.complete (the parent's post-submit close).
    onClose        -> AckAlertController.cancel (close with no mutation).
  Logic (verbatim ports):
    NOTE_MAX = 1000                        -> AckAlertProjection.noteMaxLength.
    maxLength = NOTE_MAX + 50 (1050)       -> noteInputLimit + clampToInputLimit (grapheme-safe).
    note.trim()                            -> trimmedNote (whitespacesAndNewlines).
    trimmed.length > NOTE_MAX              -> isTooLong (length = utf16.count = JS `.length`;
                                              unit-tested incl. an astral emoji = 2 units).
    onSubmit(trimmed) (empty allowed)      -> submitBody(for:) trims; empty note accepted
                                              (ack with no note; audit timeline still records).
    disabled={submitting || tooLong}       -> submitDisabled.
    error={tooLong ? noteHint : undefined} -> fieldError (the hint reused as the too-long
                                              validation copy).
    noteHint {{max: NOTE_MAX}}             -> noteHint substitutes {{max}} -> 1000.
    reset note on (re)open (useEffect)     -> resetNoteIfAlertChanged keyed by alertID + re-arm.
    submitting guard on close              -> model.cancel() no-op while submitting.
  Composition (web Modal/form -> native):
    Modal title + close "x"           -> AckAlertHeader (title + freshness chip + close).
    <p> alertTitle subtitle           -> subtitle line (Text, text-secondary), shown only
                                         when the alert title is non-empty.
    <Textarea label/placeholder/rows> -> AckNoteEditor: TextEditor (minHeight 96 ~ rows 4)
                                         + visible label + prompt overlay when empty +
                                         too-long red border; built in-surface (the shared
                                         TSTextArea's LocalizedStringKey label can't resolve
                                         the per-surface i18n table), exactly as the 0007
                                         sibling's in-surface fields.
    hint <p> (aria-describedby)       -> always-present hint line (muted; turns red as the
                                         too-long error) + a live "n/1000" grapheme counter,
                                         and the field's VoiceOver value (count of max).
    Button ghost Cancel (disabled)    -> TSButton(.ghost).disabled(submitting).
    Button primary Acknowledge        -> TSButton(.primary, isLoading: submitting)
                                         .disabled(submitDisabled).
  Native widening (honest, documented): the web parent owns the mutation + toast/undo; the
  native client additionally surfaces an acknowledge failure inline (AckErrorText) so the
  user can retry, and widens the prop-driven dialog into the prompt-required loading / empty
  / error / stale / offline envelopes (the web component is only ever rendered with a target).
  Tailwind classes were NOT ported; chrome is P1/S9 tokens (TSSpacing/TSRadius/Color.TS/
  Font.TS) via TSGlassPanel/TSFadeIn/TSButton.

==================================================================================
STATES (every state renders -- no hidden surfaces)
==================================================================================
  loading  -> AckAlertLoadingState (spinner + "Loading the alert...").
  empty    -> AckAlertEmptyState (ContentUnavailableView "No alert selected to acknowledge")
              -- the native widening of the web "dialog only opens from a row".
  error    -> AckAlertErrorState (QueryError-equivalent + Retry -> model.refresh()).
  stale    -> freshness chip "Stale" + connectivity banner + ONE guarded auto-refresh.
  offline  -> freshness chip "Offline" + banner; cached context kept; no refetch; the note
              stays editable (the ack syncs on reconnect).
  content  -> the populated form (subtitle + note editor + hint/counter + footer; + inline
              reload error if a refresh failed while a cached context remains; + the submit
              error line if the acknowledge service failed).
  Telemetry: model.start() emits P1/S11 view.opened surface="AcknowledgeAlertDialog" (once,
  idempotent -- ModelTests proven).

